WEBVTT

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.880
Oh no! You're drenched!

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.080
Akihito-san, towels! Towels!

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.920
Honestly, just where did you guys go?

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.130
Well-

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.580
While I was out walking...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:19.250
it started raining suddenly,
so I took shelter from the rain in the park.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:24.880
Then Natsuo came to pick me up,
and I guess he fell because of his leg.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:31.080
I see. Natsuo-kun, I'm sorry. Come on now, you need
to hurry and dry yourselves off and get changed.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.710
Hey, thanks... for keeping quiet...

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.420
Mijuku mujou saredo

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.420
Inexperienced, heartless, but even so,

00:00:55.210 --> 00:01:02.580
Utsukushiku are

00:00:55.210 --> 00:01:02.580
Be beautiful

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:13.540
No Destiny fusawashiku nai

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:13.540
No Destiny, unworthy

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.470
You okay...?

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.470
Did something happen...?

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.470
I'll...

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.470
Be waiting for you...

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.500
Konnanja kitto monotarinai

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.500
If it's like this, then probably things will go well

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.330
Kurai katattokeba umaku iku

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.330
If we just talk as if it's never enough

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.580
Mono, kane, ai, koto,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.580
Things, money, love, words,

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.330
I got here before you.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.330
I have the correct meeting place, right?

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.330
Did something happen? You okay?

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.330
Mou jikokenji akita

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.330
I'm tired of self-asserting myself already

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.540
Déjà vu nani ga sonna fuman nanda?

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.540
Déjà vu, what are you so unsatisfied about?

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.290
Sanzan wagamama katattoite

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.290
You've said all sorts of selfish things,

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.210
Kore ijou hoka ni nani ga iru?

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.210
what more could you possibly want?

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:37.000
Sonna tokoro mo warito kirai ja nai

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:37.000
I kind of don't mind that about you

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.630
Mou "kiki akitanda yo sono serifu"

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.630
Honestly, "I'm sick of hearing that line"

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.420
Chuuto hanpa dake ha iya

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.420
The one thing I don't want is ambiguousness

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:49.170
Mou ii aa shite kou shite ittetatte

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:49.170
Enough. Even if you say to do this or that,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.040
Aishite doushite? iwaretatte

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.040
Even if you say love me, or why?

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.830
Asobi dakenara kantan de

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.830
It's easy if it's just for fun

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.630
Shinken koushou muchakucha de

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.630
And that it's reckless serious negotiating

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.960
Omoi mo shinai omoi kotoba

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.960
How many times are those worn out unexpectedly

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.040
Nando tsukai furusu noka?

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.040
Serious words going to be used?

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:04.130
Douse kitai shitetanda deki race demo

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:04.130
We were hoping anyway, even if it was a fixed race,

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.750
Inyou darake no phrase mo

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.750
Even all those quoted phrases,

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.380
Kakato mochiagaru kotoba taboo ni shite

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.380
Making backtracking words taboo

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.500
Kuuki wo yonda ame furanaide yo

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.500
Take a hint, don't let it rain

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:17.130
Domestic Girlfriend

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.630
I... I've been in love with Sensei for a long time now...

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.670
"A long time"? Do you mean
before we even started living together?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.790
About that... Does Hina-nee know?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.920
Sensei has... reciprocated my feelings.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.960
But it's not Sensei's fault.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:55.040
I just flat-out kept pushing my feelings one-sidedly,
and she kinda gave in to that...

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.790
What do you plan on doing, from here on...?

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:04.330
In the future... I want to be with Sensei.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.500
You serious...?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.420
Yeah.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.040
I see...

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:20.580
H-hey.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.290
Hey...

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.710
This...

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.420
This'll be the last time, so...

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.580
Natsuo-kun, dinner's ready.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.670
Oh, thank you very much.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.670
I believe you like it, right? Ginger-fried pork.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:48.500
It's late, but it really helped that Rui
had already done most of the preparations.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:18.710
M-morning...

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.500
Morning.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.540
Yesterday's ginger-fried pork was good...

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.500
I see.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.330
Hey, I decided on something.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.080
Huh?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.000
I'm going to start disliking you from now on.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.000
I gave it some thought.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.920
There are often people who head towards disliking
the person they liked, or even hating them,

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.500
and I wondered why.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.500
But I think I kinda understand now.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.920
To come to dislike someone is a type of self-defense.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:57.290
By "disliking" the cause of what makes one suffer,
one's heart starts to feel better, so...

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:03.330
I'll still act normally to you as family.
Mom did ask me to anyway.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.040
I'll also help you while your leg's still healing.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:10.210
But... from now on, I'm going
to make an effort to dislike you, that's all...

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.210
Did the handouts get passed all the way to the back?

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.380
I'm sure there were quite a few of you
who had been looking at the yearly calendar

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.000
and eagerly looking forward to this,
but finally, next month is the school trip.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:29.130
The destination is Okinawa.
For this time only, swimsuits are also allowed.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.080
You'll get to see me, your teacher, in a speedo.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.170
Ew! Seriously? Gross!

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.540
That sucks.
Hey, what's up?

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.250
You look like your shit's all blocked up or something.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.420
It's Okinawa! It's swimsuits!

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.210
Y-yeah. Sounds like fun...

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.250
Over here...

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.540
How's Rui doing? I tried messaging her on LINE,
but it says she hasn't read it.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:55.540
After that incident, I told her everything.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:00.460
And then Rui said that she was going
to start disliking me...

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:12.000
Because of this... things aren't going
to end between us, are they?

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.790
You were able to take your cast off.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:37.920
Yeah, fortunately. I somehow made it
in time for the school trip.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.750
Then we'll all be able to swim
in the ocean together. Right, Rui-Rui?

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.080
Well, I...

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.380
I wanna see Rui-chan in a swimsuit!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.460
I don't know how I can ever
make it up to you for what happened.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:51.330
That doesn't matter anymore, really.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.750
Hey, everyone.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.420
I'm glad that you're all here.
The results of the contest are in.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.710
The official announcement won't
happen until a little later,

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:06.420
but to my delight, we have an award winner
from our Literature Club.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.040
What?!

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.000
Really?!

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:12.130
Although we are only a school club, it is quite the honor
to receive an honorable mention award.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.250
Who? Who is it?

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.040
The award winner this time is...

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.880
Rui Tachibana-kun.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.670
That's awesome! Rui-Rui, congratulations!

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.420
Fantastic! Congratulations, Rui!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.420
This was the first time you wrote a story, right?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:28.380
Yeah...

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.710
And the fact that it was
THAT interesting is amazing! I know!

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.580
Let's have a party!
A party to celebrate Rui-chan winning an award!

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.460
Sounds good!

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.630
Right, Nat-chan?!

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.960
Huh? Oh, sure...

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:41.130
It's a happy occasion, so let's go all out.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.250
Yeeeah!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:50.580
Fujii-kun.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.000
Actually, I'm pretty depressed.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.580
Fujii-kun, you too, right?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.540
I wonder if having talent or not is a big deal after all...

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:10.630
I've liked reading books since I was little and...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.710
around when I was in middle school,
I tried entering a public picture book contest,

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.210
and I received the lowest honorable mention award.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.830
I thought that even I could do it,
and so I kept entering one after another, but...

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:24.540
I learned a lesson that there is always someone better...

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.290
So then I decided to think of it this way.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:35.210
That even those without talent still must have
that "something" that people with talent can't feel.

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:39.210
I think that depressed feeling right now
will come in handy someday.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:42.040
Probably, something like this will occur
a lot from here on as well.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.000
Let's take this unfulfilled feeling
and draw all the experience we can from it,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.750
and keep on working hard together!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.080
Yeah...

