00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.290
Call

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.290
End

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.290
Yes?

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:05.960
What brings you here at this late hour?

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:07.420
Sensei...

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.880
please make me your apprentice!

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:12.880
I'm not interested at this time.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.880
This isn't like a sales call!

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:18.830
Please let go. I don't do that kind of thing.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:22.830
Please at least hear me out, Sensei!
You Hasukawa-sensei!

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.960
Please don't shout my pen name.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.290
So...

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.830
What is this about?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.000
You show up suddenly uninvited
and then you ask to be my apprentice...?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:35.670
I'm already your advisor, you know?

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:42.040
Today's award announcement was...
well... to be honest, it was a huge shock and...

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:46.920
I want to become a novelist no matter what...!
So that I can make a living by writing novels!

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:51.290
Well... I kind of knew that was probably your dream but...

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:56.880
I kind of felt like my own lack of talent
was being flaunted at me... But I can't give up!

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:00.210
So, I was hoping that maybe I could
study under you, Sensei...

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:05.170
I see. So, you feel there is a difference in talent
between you and Tachibana-kun, and you're flustered.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.040
Tachibana-kun came to say
that she wanted to decline the award.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.420
Decline...? Why...?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:15.290
I don't know, she didn't say the reason why.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.080
I understand your impatience.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:24.250
However, if what you call "talent" is a measure
of the "likelihood of becoming an author,"

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.960
then I think that you have more "talent."

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:33.460
The reason is simple. It's because you have
a strong desire to "become an author."

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:36.880
No matter how much expressiveness
or intuitive sense you have,

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.130
it doesn't amount to anything if you don't have
the resolve to keep continuing on with that.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:46.380
While even if you only have average potential, your
chance will come if you continue to keep working hard.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:52.130
Keeping that in mind,
in regards to my answer to your request...

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.250
it's not even worth answering.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.210
What?!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.710
I am utterly amazed to hear that
from someone who wants to be a novelist.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:02.460
Just how many works have you written anyway?

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:09.960
Supposing that you apprenticed under me,
you may learn a few things about the industry, but...

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:14.210
in the end, the only way is for you
to struggle by yourself and keep on writing.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:19.500
Fujii-kun.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.040
Do you want to write novels?

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:26.250
Or do you want the status of being a "novelist"?

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:29.920
Welcome home.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.210
H-hey...

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.250
Oh yeah. I still hadn't properly said anything...

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.830
Congratulations on winning
the honorable mention award.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.130
I'm not very happy about it.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.000
Don't say that. It's an award
you received after all that effort.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:55.380
Kiriya-sensei's words totally hit the mark,

00:11:55.380 --> 00:12:00.630
and I feel like all my pitifulness
and thoughtlessness got found out...

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:06.960
I'm... so lame...

